#Variable Matches: subject_id = patient id, hadm_id = hospital admission 
At this stage, I can either merge by subject_id (unique patient identifier) or hadm_id (specific hospital admission identifier). In this specific case, understanding the factors that may impact a patients survival within a 24 hour admission period requires us to consider specifically the hospital admission id, rather than the cumulative information stored within a patient id.

df = icu.merge(admissions, on=['subject_id', 'hadm_id'])
df

df = df.merge(patients, on='subject_id')
df

# merging chartevents/vitals will be far more difficult since its raw form is massive
df_24hr = df[['subject_id','hadm_id','icustay_id','intime']] #selecting the identifiers for each individual dataset
vitals_filtered = vitals.merge(df_24hr, on = ['subject_id','hadm_id','icustay_id'])

vitals_filtered['charttime'] = pd.to_datetime(vitals_filtered['charttime']) 
vitals_filtered['intime'] = pd.to_datetime(vitals_filtered['intime'])

vitals_filtered = vitals_filtered[
    vitals_filtered['charttime'] <= vitals_filtered['intime'] + pd.Timedelta(hours=24)
]

